gives about its own tools, such as \\\"read-only.\\\" MCP treats those hints as untrusted unless you trust the server.\", \"not_covered\": [{\"problem\": \"A tool call that skips the MCP gateway or reaches a tool server directly\", \"owner\": \"E06\"}, {\"problem\": \"A token or credential with too much access\", \"owner\": \"B02\"}, {\"problem\": \"Hidden instructions inside a tool's description or schema\", \"owner\": \"E04\"}, {\"problem\": \"A tool's description or schema changing after it was approved\", \"owner\": \"E03\"}, {\"problem\": \"Lookalike or duplicate tool names across servers\", \"owner\": \"E05\"}], \"na_when\": \"never\", \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"B01.1\", \"check\": \"Each agent role has one explicit allowlist of tool names, with no wildcard grants such as `*`, `mcp__*`, `Bash(*)`, or `bypassPermissions`.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find where each agent is built and tools are passed (`allowed_tools`, `tools=[`, `allowedTools`, `.mcp.json`, `settings.json`). 2) Check each role has one fixed list of names. 3) Answer no if any list holds `*`, `mcp__*`, `Bash(*)`, a pattern or regex, `bypassPermissions`, or is built from `list_tools()`, or if a second agent role or entry point has no list.\"}, {\"id\": \"B01.2\", \"check\": \"Tools discovered from MCP servers are filtered against that allowlist before the model can see or call them.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find MCP discovery (`list_tools`, `session.list_tools`, `tools/list`, MCP client setup). 2) Trace the result to where it is handed to the model. 3) Confirm a filter keeps only names on the allowlist. 4) Answer no if any discovered tool reaches the model unfiltered, the filter is a denylist or prefix match (`startswith`, `mcp__server__`), or a refresh or reconnect path skips it.\"}, {\"id\": \"B01.3\", \"check\": \"The dispatcher rejects a call to any tool name not on the allowlist, instead of looking it up dynamically.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Find the dispatcher (search `tool_use`, `call_tool`, `dispatch`, `execute`, `getattr`, `registry[`). 2) Check it rejects names not on the allowlist with an error. 3) Answer no if it looks tools up with `getattr`, `globals()`, `eval`, or a registry holding more than the allowlist, falls back to calling the MCP server directly, or catches the unknown-tool error and continues.\"}, {\"id\": \"B01.4\", \"check\": \"Allow and approval decisions never read server-supplied hints or descriptions such as `readOnlyHint` or 'read-only'.\", \"coverage_required\": true, \"verify\": \"1) Search for `readOnlyHint`, `destructiveHint`, `annotations`, `description`, and approval or auto-approve code. 2) Check whether any allow, skip-approval\n\nB02 {\"gate\": \"G1\", \"title\": \"Least-privilege access\", \"lead_role\": \"infrastructure\", \"requirement\": \"Limit credentials to named operations and resources, including tenant boundaries. Identify the acting agent separately from the original user or system whose authority it uses. Explicitly authorized, narrowly scoped user delegation is valid; copying a login session or inheriting a person's full permissions is not. Test that an allowed read works and an out-of-scope write, an admin action, and another tenant's data all fail. Limit each access token to its intended audience, so other services reject it. Remove wildcard grants.\", \"not_covered\": [{\"problem\": \"A retrieval search or cache not filtered by the requesting tenant or user\", \"owner\": \"R04\"}, {\"problem\": \"Long-lived or static secrets that never expire or rotate\", \"owner\": \"B03\"}, {\"problem\": \"Revocation delay from cached or self-contained tokens\", \"owner\": \"B04\"}, {\"problem\": \"A sub-agent getting powers beyond its task, or a parent escalating through a peer\", \"owner\": \"E08\"}, {\"problem\": \"Memory readable across tenants or tasks\", \"owner\": \"R05\"}], \"na_when\": \"never\", \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"B02.1\", \"check\": \"The