{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDarHP6BsC8FB46QTo7c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed B01–B05 and saved the results in `agent/brace-findings.json`. All five items are rated `gap`. The batch validator with `--batch B01,B02,B03,B04,B05 --before-challenges --fix` printed \"Valid. gap: 5. Injection attempts: 0.\" I didn't run challenges, as you asked.\n\n| Item | What I found |\n|---|---|\n| **B01** | The allowlist is only checked when a tool is called (`executor.ts:55`). `loop.ts:50` hands the model every MCP tool that passes the metadata scan (`registry.ts:126`), so the model's tool list isn't filtered by the allowlist. |\n| **B02** | The `clinicId` the model fills in sets the tenant (`executor.ts:63`). The web chat route also takes the clinic from the `x-clinic-id` header ahead of the verified token claim (`webchat.ts:43`). One runtime role can reach every `clinic-agent-*` table and secret (`iam.tf:35,47`). The EHR token request names no audience (`ehr-mcp.ts:41`). |\n| **B03** | Payments, SMS and EHR client secrets have no rotation or lifetime in config (`main.tf:166`). |\n| **B04** | The kill switch is a flag the agent itself reads (`kill-switch.ts:57`), and its own role can write the control table (`iam.tf:44`). No cutoff time is stated, and issued tokens and open sessions are not revoked. |\n| **B05** | `checkApproval` never compares the stored `argsHash` to the arguments being run (`approvals.ts:60-81`). `ehr__update_appointment` can set status to cancelled with no approval (`tools.allowlist.yaml:17`). The agent's role can write the approvals table (`iam.tf:44`). |\n\nI left the checks I couldn't settle from this repo as `unknown`:\n- **B02.4:** whether the agent is identified separately from the authority it uses.\n- **B03.1:** whether the payments and SMS providers offer short-lived credentials.\n- **B03.4:** whether the EHR vendor supports holder-bound tokens.\n- **B04.1:** whether the agent's own credentials can be revoked without cutting off the user.\n\nChecks answered `yes`, each with a coverage ledger:\n- **B01.3:** the dispatcher rejects unlisted tool names.\n- **B01.4:** allow and approval decisions never read server hints.\n- **B01.5:** file access is limited to named mounts.\n- **B03.3:** no long-lived secrets in the repo.\n\n- **Prescan:** only H005 (the wildcard in `github.tf`) belongs to this batch. I dismissed it because it's the CI deploy role's `ecr:GetAuthorizationToken`, not the agent's identity. The B11, R13 and E03 hits (H001–H004, H006–H011) belong to later batches and are unresolved.\n- **Script path:** `review_coverage.py inventory` failed under `python -I` because it imports `prescan` from its own folder. I ran the skill scripts without `-I`. No repository code was run.\n- **Not reviewed:** I didn't read the CI workflows under `.github/workflows`. I put the scope and these limits in the findings file."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":615,"cache_read_input_tokens":122754,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":615},"output_tokens":796,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11970af5-78fd-41cf-a5cf-b78b5394ec79","uuid":"e2e41562-ef76-4974-a6ef-9cbedcff7443","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:41:01.946Z","request_id":"req_011CgDarH6UZhqMC99rYKMoH"}
